    "constrains": "the per-joint generator bias; the sum of retroflexion, rotation and anteflexion, also given separately",
    "source": "de Vries, Visser and Prechtl 1985, Early Hum Dev 12:99-120, doi:10.1016/0378-3782(85)90174-4, scatter figures read into companion/sources/deVries1985_extract.md; median at 12 weeks, at 13 weeks, lowest and highest fetus over both (Figs. 15-17)"
   },
   "arm_motion_pct": {
    "role": "FIT (derived)",
    "constrains": "how busy the generators are between counted movements",
    "source": "derived: general movement share plus isolated arm movements per hour x their duration (1.64 to 1.89 s): 11.5 + 48 x 1.64 / 36 = 13.7 at 12 weeks, 12.5 + 51.5 x 1.64 / 36 = 14.8 at 13 weeks; lowest 6 + 6 x 1.64 / 36 = 6.3, highest 18 + 104 x 1.89 / 36 = 23.5. de Vries, Visser and Prechtl 1985, Early Hum Dev 12:99-120, doi:10.1016/0378-3782(85)90174-4, scatter figures read into companion/sources/deVries1985_extract.md; median at 12 weeks, at 13 weeks, lowest and highest fetus over both; Zoia et al. 2013, PLoS One 8:e80876, doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0080876, full text read; 14 weeks, wrist tracked at 4 Hz"
